# Copy to .env.local and fill in from the Coveo admin console once org access is granted.
# Admin console > Organization > API Keys, and the org ID shown in the top-right org switcher.
#
# Two different kinds of values here, split by trust boundary (see
# docs/adr/0005-server-token-and-passage-routes.md):
#
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the client JS bundle at build time and
#   are visible to anyone who opens devtools. Only the org ID belongs here —
#   it's not a secret, it's just which org to talk to.
# - COVEO_API_KEY is a privileged, server-only key (Search - Execute queries,
#   Analytics - Push, ML - Allow content preview). It is read only by Route
#   Handlers under src/app/api/ (token minting, passage retrieval) and must
#   NEVER be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ or it would ship to the browser.

# Client-side (safe to expose in the browser bundle)
NEXT_PUBLIC_COVEO_ORGANIZATION_ID=

# Server-only (never exposed to the client — used by src/app/api/token and
# src/app/api/passages to mint short-lived search tokens / call Passage
# Retrieval on the user's behalf)
COVEO_API_KEY=
